  "mechanisms": [
    "Cognitive processes of short-term memory and attention operating in tasks were impaired by more bluish light ('cool' and artificial 'daylight') compared to 'warm' white lighting.",
    "Selective operations and capacity limits of attention in problem solving were enhanced by 'warm' compared to 'cool' and artificial 'daylight' white lighting.",
    "Gender differences in emotional reaction to colour of light may be attributable to the socialization of gender differences in emotional experience and functioning (Knez & Kers, 2000)."
  ],
  "moderators": [
    "gender"
  ],
  "implementation_implications": [
    "The findings suggest that 'warm' white lighting may be beneficial for short-term recall and problem-solving tasks."
  ],
